* pattern_bt.sno
* Bottleneck: pattern backtracking with alternation.
* Alternation of 4 choices + SPAN, 8,000,000 iterations -- the RTX-8 GRADED window.
* WHY 8M AND NOT 4M (s220, measured): warm and cold differ 2.3x on this program (hugepage compaction, s201
* class).  s219 recorded "4M ~ 870 ms" from a COLD read; WARM, 2M is ~400 ms and 4M ~800 ms, i.e. AT the
* MIN_MS=800 floor rather than clear of it.  8M gives ~1.6 s warm.  Apply MIN_MS to the WARM window or every
* rung grades on a cold flier.  MIN-OF-N, DISCARD RUN 1: single runs here swing up to 4.7x, medians are
* worthless, and only the minimum reproduced across two independent harness layouts (1.136x vs 1.135x).
* Checksum is input-determined and was PREDICTED IN ADVANCE: result == K, W == ccccddddaaaa at every K.
    &TRIM = 1
    &STLIMIT = 1000000000
    &ANCHOR = 0
    PAT = ('aaa' | 'bbb' | 'ccc' | 'ddd') SPAN('abcd') . W
    S = 'xxxxxxxxxxbbbccccddddaaaaxxxxxxxxxxbbbccccddddaaaa'
    T1 = TIME()
    N = 0
LOOP    S PAT                           :F(DONE)
    N = LT(N, 8000000) N + 1            :S(LOOP)
DONE    T2 = TIME()
    OUTPUT = "result: " N
    OUTPUT = "W: " W
    OUTPUT = "ms: " (T2 - T1)
END
